WEBVTT

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:04.060
<i>Speed and angle for Earth entry are on target.</i>

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:10.070
<b><i>#ENCODERGASM PRESENTS</i></b>

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:06.150
<i>All machines, please provide a systems check prior to atmospheric entry.</i>

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:07.360
<i>FLAT One, all green.</i>

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:08.770
FLAT Two, all green.

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:10.150
<i>FLAT Three, all green.</i>

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:11.570
<i>FLAT Four, all green.</i>

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:12.950
<i>FLAT Five, all green.</i>

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:14.280
<i>FLAT Six, all green.</i>

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:17.200
<i>{c&\a6}"Mary had a little lamb..."</i>

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:20.620
<i>{c&\a6}"'Baa, Baa' ... little lamb..."</i>

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:18.870
Close your face guards.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:23.620
<i>- "Mary had a little lamb..." 
 - "London Bridge is falling down..." 
 - "One little, two little, three little Moonrace..."</i>

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:27.630
<i>{c&\a6}- "Her fleece was white as snow." 
 - "Falling down, falling down. London Bridge is falling down..." 
 - "...four little, five little, six little Moonrace..."</i>

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:33.050
<i>{c&HFFFFFF&\a6}- "And everywhere that Mary went..." 
 - "...my fair lady." 
 - "...seven little, eight little, nine little Moonrace..."</i>

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:40.010
<i>{c&\a6}- "Mary went, Mary went..." 
 - "Take a key and lock her up, lock her up, lock her up." 
 - "...ten little Moonrace boys. Ten little, nine little,"</i>

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:42.100
<i>{c&\a6}- "And everywhere that Mary went..." 
 - "Take a key and..." 
 - "eight little..."</i>

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:41.990
<b>Howl to the Moon</b>

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:46.870
That's hot, Loran!

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:48.170
But it's so interesting.

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:49.380
Is it gonna be alright?

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:52.380
Yeah. Nobody's gonna know who we are.

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:55.170
Keith, Loran, take care of yourselves now!

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:56.550
You too, Fran Doll!

00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:58.260
Don't overwork yourself, Loran!

00:01:58.260 --> 00:01:59.970
Thanks, Keith.

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:43.260
<i>Looks like you missed, Lord Guin!</i>

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:45.350
<i>You let it go on purpose, didn't you?!</i>

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:47.060
The coyote got away!

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:49.270
You think that boy's alright?

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:55.070
<i>You're as good as your reputation suggests, Lord Guin.</i>

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:58.780
Take care, boy!

00:03:55.170 --> 00:03:58.460
"Mary had a little lamb..."

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:22.440
Sis!

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:24.570
That kid's drowning!

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:25.780
Jessica!

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:31.160
Jessica! Sam! Go downstream!

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:33.370
Sam!

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:34.250
I'm on it!

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:53.140
He seems to be doing better now.

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:54.980
He should be alright now.

00:05:02.650 --> 00:05:03.860
Cut that out!

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:11.370
He must have started drowning 'cause he was chasing after this.

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:14.870
It's not exactly unusual for foreigners to come here.

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:16.870
Jessica! Take care of him, alright?

00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:18.750
Yes, My Lady.

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:39.860
Eat.

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:47.860
If you hadn't been drowning...

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:51.450
the Heim Family wouldn't put up with a foreigner like yourself.

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:53.580
Lady Sochie,

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:55.750
you'd better not get too close to these kinds of people.

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:13.850
I don't need charity from you. I still have some money.

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:15.850
I understand, Loran Cehack.

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:19.650
But you don't have enough.

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:22.770
Then I'll work to pay it off.

00:06:22.770 --> 00:06:24.860
Were you looking through my bag?

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:27.440
You were checking us out before.

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:29.860
I was drowning, so I couldn't really see anything.

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:31.660
What a shame.

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:33.660
Is that so?

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:36.580
You were more interested in this than us!

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:38.250
Give that back! It's mine!

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:39.160
No way!

00:06:39.160 --> 00:06:40.460
Come on!

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:43.670
What are you doing this evening?

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:45.880
Well, the Heim Mine's in this town,

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:47.670
so I thought I'd settle down somewhere around here.

00:06:49.170 --> 00:06:50.470
So you <i>do</i> have a plan in mind.

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:52.470
Heim Mine...

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:54.760
Is this Mister Heim's house?

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:55.680
Yep.

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:56.970
Caharan!

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:02.270
May I go?

00:07:02.270 --> 00:07:03.560
Fine.

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:14.580
This...

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:18.250
She really <i>does</i> look like Her Majesty Dianna.

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:22.880
I was washing up to for the Coming of Age Ceremony,

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:25.040
...but you went and spoiled it.

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:26.960
I apologize!

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:34.850
l asked my father to give you a job in his mine.

00:07:34.850 --> 00:07:36.680
Thank you very much! I mean it!

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:41.270
I had no idea the river was so fierce,

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:42.770
so I almost drowned.

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:45.480
But you saved me. Thank you very much!

00:07:45.860 --> 00:07:47.360
- I'll be but a moment.
- Ma'am.

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:57.450
Aren't you going as well?

00:07:57.450 --> 00:07:58.740
Really? Where to?

00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:00.160
To the ceremony!

00:08:11.550 --> 00:08:12.970
Vehicles aren't allowed here!

00:08:19.260 --> 00:08:21.140
To the Mountain Cycle!

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:24.270
<i>To the Mountain Cycle!</i>

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:26.270
C'mon!

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:33.650
C'mon.

00:08:33.650 --> 00:08:35.070
Is that your sister?

00:08:35.070 --> 00:08:36.160
Yeah.

00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:43.660
In two years, I'll--

00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:46.170
This is as far as you two go, Milady.

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:48.540
I can't let you go up there this evening.

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:50.670
They make the ceremony last the entire night.

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:52.460
I'm fifteen too.

00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:53.760
Foreigners can't--

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:55.180
- Hey!
- Loran!

00:08:55.180 --> 00:08:56.470
Milady!

00:08:56.470 --> 00:08:59.350
This is as far as foreigners are allowed to go!

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:09.570
You'll get sent back down if you get caught.

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:15.570
Now, the Coming of Age Ceremony will begin!

00:09:15.570 --> 00:09:18.070
All of you who are already adults, please leave!

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:20.580
Is that the White Doll?

00:09:21.950 --> 00:09:24.080
Adults, leave the mountain! Leave now!

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:26.960
Loran!

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:37.760
Loran!

00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:39.680
Don't break the taboo!

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:41.050
Come back!

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:51.770
You may choose my partner!

00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:17.970
It's papa's new model... Incredible!

00:10:23.970 --> 00:10:26.480
Race time! Lets see just how fast this thing can go!

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:31.770
Fine! I'll show you what this new model can do!

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:41.370
One, two!

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:44.870
You're slow! Hurry up and get ready!

00:10:45.450 --> 00:10:46.660
Where's Loran?

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:48.870
Over by the elevator to the new seam.

00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:54.250
Loran, stop what you're working on!

00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:55.750
O-okay!

00:10:55.750 --> 00:10:57.460
Mister Heim needs to see you.

00:10:57.460 --> 00:10:59.050
The Master does?

00:10:59.050 --> 00:11:03.050
He heard talk that you're pretty good with machines.

00:11:10.270 --> 00:11:13.150
<i>This is Lord Guin's newest-model car.</i>

00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:17.440
Excuse me... I'm Loran Cehack.

00:11:17.440 --> 00:11:20.860
<i>He wants to convert this model into a sports car.</i>

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:23.570
Whoa! This opens up to become more seats!

00:11:23.570 --> 00:11:25.660
Lord Guin asked for that addition.

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:29.160
It's so shiny!

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:30.960
Isn't this cool, sis?

00:11:30.960 --> 00:11:33.250
I already saw it.

00:11:34.170 --> 00:11:36.670
<i>Do we really need fighter planes?</i>

00:11:36.670 --> 00:11:39.050
<i>I've considered the possibility of us fighting over water.</i>

00:11:39.050 --> 00:11:41.260
<i>If people from the Gaurian continent invaded,</i>

00:11:41.260 --> 00:11:42.760
<i>then I suppose that'd be necessary.</i>

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:45.470
<i>Then that justifies their continued production.</i>

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:47.760
<i>That's enough for now.</i>

00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:49.980
<i>This could soon affect the other mountain areas as well,</i>

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:51.480
<i>so think it over.</i>

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:55.860
There's been talk, but are you sure that we're really going to war?

00:11:55.860 --> 00:11:57.480
It's just a rumor.

00:11:57.480 --> 00:11:58.780
Then again, this could be precisely the opportunity

00:11:58.780 --> 00:12:01.950
I've sought to industrialize our society.

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:03.450
That's the heir for you.

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:07.370
You're using your position as the family heir for development and industry.

00:12:07.370 --> 00:12:09.750
My father was a politician and a diplomat,

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:11.250
and thus so am I.

00:12:11.960 --> 00:12:13.960
Loran is here...

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:16.040
So you came, I see.

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:18.460
Loran Cehack.

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:22.170
From this point onward, I am appointing you as our chauffeur.

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:23.970
A private chauffeur?

00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:26.350
That's great, Loran!

00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:28.680
Father...

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:32.140
You'll be using your time to attend the University to study.

00:12:32.140 --> 00:12:36.560
You'll soon have a hand in constructing Lord Rhineford's new era.

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:38.650
- That hair color...
- Sir?

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:40.860
I remember it.

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:44.860
You've got the same color hair as that boy who was attacked by a wolf.

00:12:47.450 --> 00:12:49.660
Thank you very much for that!

00:12:49.660 --> 00:12:51.950
I couldn't kill it, so I was worried about you.

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:52.950
Thanks to you,

00:12:52.950 --> 00:12:55.250
these two girls here were able to later rescue me.

00:12:56.080 --> 00:12:57.250
It must be fate.

00:12:57.250 --> 00:13:00.750
Then you'll study even harder to repay the heir here, will you not?

00:13:00.750 --> 00:13:03.050
- Yes!
- I'm happy for you, Loran.

00:13:03.050 --> 00:13:06.050
But keep in mind that your studies of these new things will be difficult.

00:13:06.050 --> 00:13:06.840
Right.

00:13:06.840 --> 00:13:09.180
lsn't that right, Lord Guin?

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:13.060
Yes, although it seems your father has taken a liking to Laura.

00:13:13.060 --> 00:13:15.140
I'll ask for permission for him attend the Coming of Age Ceremony this year,

00:13:15.140 --> 00:13:17.770
since he's already two years late. Alright?

00:13:17.770 --> 00:13:19.980
M-may I really?!

00:13:19.980 --> 00:13:21.270
With me?!

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:24.070
I brought the new car outside.

00:13:24.070 --> 00:13:27.070
I'm looking forward to seeing what you can do, Laura Cehack.

00:13:27.070 --> 00:13:28.280
Lord Guin!

00:13:29.070 --> 00:13:30.160
Lord Guin,

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:32.660
Is that them? The Militia Air Force?

00:13:32.660 --> 00:13:35.660
Mr. Kune is a genius with airplanes.

00:13:36.370 --> 00:13:38.250
He's the one in the fastest plane,

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:40.460
leading the others in formation.

00:13:40.460 --> 00:13:42.250
Hit the gas!

00:13:42.880 --> 00:13:43.960
Just like that.

00:13:43.960 --> 00:13:46.260
Keep it in place until the thermometer is centered.

00:13:49.340 --> 00:13:51.970
Oh, right. Miss Kihel,

00:13:51.970 --> 00:13:53.350
I'd like you to join us at the castle's summer party.

00:13:53.350 --> 00:13:54.980
At Bostonia Castle!?

00:13:54.980 --> 00:13:56.270
Of course.

00:13:56.270 --> 00:13:58.350
Unless your parents are against it, that is.

00:13:58.350 --> 00:14:02.360
Not at all. It'd be our pleasure to have my daughter's social debut at Bostonia Castle.

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:34.260
Lord Guin kept referring to Loran as "Laura."

00:14:38.060 --> 00:14:40.980
Not too great. I guess that's why they're only Militia soldiers.

00:14:40.980 --> 00:14:44.360
Get everyone together under the airship!

00:14:44.780 --> 00:14:46.360
Colonel! Can I come?

00:14:46.360 --> 00:14:48.450
What business do you have with the heir?

00:14:48.450 --> 00:14:50.780
Well, he's the guy who purchased dad's planes.

00:14:50.780 --> 00:14:55.450
Don't be silly. I was the one who recommended your father's planes, Miashei.

00:14:55.450 --> 00:14:58.370
The heir just gave him the money for it, that's all.

00:14:59.460 --> 00:15:00.750
Papa!

00:15:09.170 --> 00:15:11.680
Don't worry about limited numbers, we're mass producing them.

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:13.260
You can use this car.

00:15:13.260 --> 00:15:15.180
Thank you, sir!

00:15:15.180 --> 00:15:19.140
You're a good driver. I have high expectations for you, Laura.

00:15:19.640 --> 00:15:20.560
Yes, sir!

00:15:20.560 --> 00:15:21.770
Bye!

00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:24.650
It's "Loran," right?

00:15:24.650 --> 00:15:25.860
Yep. "Loran."

00:15:31.950 --> 00:15:33.660
Start up the motor!

00:16:20.370 --> 00:16:22.660
I'll be back soon. Please wait for me here.

00:16:22.660 --> 00:16:23.670
Ma'am.

00:16:25.170 --> 00:16:26.250
I'm not going.

00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:27.750
Why not?

00:16:27.750 --> 00:16:31.760
Who wants to get stuck watching your sister buy accessories for <i>her</i> party?

00:16:32.670 --> 00:16:35.050
That store only suits the taste of elite rich snobs.

00:16:35.050 --> 00:16:37.760
Miss Kihel has very good taste.

00:16:37.760 --> 00:16:40.680
Loran, you're always praising my sister.

00:17:09.170 --> 00:17:10.880
You seem to be doing well for yourself.

00:17:10.880 --> 00:17:12.880
You too, Keith. Do you work at this bakery?

00:17:12.880 --> 00:17:13.970
Yeah.

00:17:13.970 --> 00:17:15.970
Fran's working here in Nocis too.

00:17:15.970 --> 00:17:17.680
You're waiting for Fran?

00:17:17.680 --> 00:17:19.180
Check it out.

00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:21.850
I'm working at the Heim house in Vicinity Town.

00:17:22.350 --> 00:17:25.270
Do you have a friend working here in Nocis City?

00:17:25.270 --> 00:17:27.980
He's a good friend from my hometown.

00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:30.570
Is everything alright?

00:17:34.280 --> 00:17:35.950
Did you finish your music homework?

00:17:35.950 --> 00:17:37.160
Of course.

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:39.950
It's a waste of time to get scolded by the teacher.

00:17:46.250 --> 00:17:49.960
I'm sorry. I'm in a hurry and need to leave early.

00:17:49.960 --> 00:17:51.960
It's okay. See you next week.

00:17:51.960 --> 00:17:53.170
Take care.

00:17:56.050 --> 00:17:57.550
Miss Kihel Heim!

00:18:03.680 --> 00:18:05.350
Loran? He's not here?

00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:37.470
Good to see you, man!

00:18:37.470 --> 00:18:39.050
You were there the whole time?!

00:18:39.550 --> 00:18:41.550
Huh? A friend?

00:18:41.550 --> 00:18:42.850
Been taking care of yourself?

00:18:42.850 --> 00:18:45.060
Of course. How about you, Keith?

00:18:45.060 --> 00:18:47.350
What are they talking about?

00:18:47.350 --> 00:18:49.850
I love the way stirring flower feels!

00:18:49.850 --> 00:18:50.650
Ow!

00:18:53.980 --> 00:18:55.360
This is delicious!

00:18:55.360 --> 00:18:56.860
Yeah.

00:18:56.860 --> 00:18:58.360
Where's Fran Doll?

00:18:58.360 --> 00:18:59.780
On her way.

00:19:00.360 --> 00:19:01.370
Hey!

00:19:01.370 --> 00:19:02.660
Fran!

00:19:03.280 --> 00:19:05.160
Huh? Is that a girl?!

00:19:05.160 --> 00:19:06.580
Loran!

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:09.250
I guess he's getting together with some old friends.

00:19:09.250 --> 00:19:10.960
I've missed you!

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:12.880
It's good to see you too!

00:19:14.040 --> 00:19:16.760
- Isn't Keith's bread delicious? 
 - Yeah.

00:19:16.760 --> 00:19:19.550
So Fran, I heard you're working in a newspaper printing house.

00:19:19.550 --> 00:19:23.180
That's right. I can never get rid of this ink smell.

00:19:23.550 --> 00:19:24.850
I think it smells good.

00:19:25.260 --> 00:19:27.350
Is that girl asking him for a kiss?!

00:19:27.350 --> 00:19:28.350
But hey,

00:19:28.350 --> 00:19:30.980
we're all a lot more confident about living on Earth now.

00:19:30.980 --> 00:19:32.770
Careful! Don't say that out loud!

00:19:32.770 --> 00:19:34.060
But...

00:19:34.060 --> 00:19:37.440
I thought I'd be able to get real time news working for a newspaper,

00:19:37.440 --> 00:19:39.950
But there's no news about the moon at all.

00:19:39.950 --> 00:19:42.780
There are rumors that the continent of Guaria might attack us,

00:19:42.780 --> 00:19:44.280
but they really mean the moon, right?

00:19:45.080 --> 00:19:46.660
Now I get it!

00:19:46.660 --> 00:19:49.960
Loran, how's "it"? Is it all right?

00:19:49.960 --> 00:19:51.750
I haven't had time off work to check it out.

00:19:51.750 --> 00:19:54.170
That FLAT buried itself deep in the valley.

00:19:54.170 --> 00:19:56.750
There's no way anyone could find it.

00:19:56.750 --> 00:19:59.670
What are they looking at? Those three...

00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:02.550
I'm worried that an earthquake could unearth it, but...

00:20:02.550 --> 00:20:04.680
You can use a car, right?

00:20:04.680 --> 00:20:07.180
That's right. You're the closest. Go check it out.

00:20:08.560 --> 00:20:11.270
Don't be ridiculous.

00:20:21.860 --> 00:20:23.070
Caharan!

00:20:24.570 --> 00:20:27.160
I heard he left to repair that truck on the mountain.

00:20:31.660 --> 00:20:32.960
It's going the other way!

00:20:35.670 --> 00:20:38.380
We should probably turn off the headlights.

00:20:47.680 --> 00:20:54.560
<i>E mi et le, escontina</i>

00:20:54.560 --> 00:21:01.860
<i>O plenitas, o colindia</i>

00:21:01.860 --> 00:21:09.080
<i>Mi mortis sicle ha juus costro</i>

